\ Gate gaps selected from arbitrary-precision signed gate INDICES.
\ A gate index is a count from zero, not a calendar-day coordinate.
\ For index n != 0, the source sauce is (Foundation, Foundation+n).
\ The zero index is Foundation itself and has NO preceding/following
\ gap. Its interval length is set to zero without making a sauce.
\ This implementation uses the same bowl 1 / seal 1 reader as the
\ existing native gate-gap routine; result lies from 42 to 963.
\
\ Even when the signed index exceeds native 32-bit integer bounds,
\ both sauce dates and all five counters remain wide signed values.
\ This is a building block: the gate-position walker still uses
\ native indices and coordinates and has not been migrated.
\ Large inputs may require substantial exact-decimal computation.
\ No CAL compiler run has validated this module yet.

\ Typed, unambiguous scratch name: the Foundation magnitude is wide
\ decimal text, never a native calendar-day number.
The wgfoundationdigits is a wide quantity.

To prepare wide gate sauce counters given a wide signed day:
  Put "15055671" into the wgfoundationdigits.
  Set the wide calendar example's calculation day from the wgfoundationdigits given -1.
  Put the wide calendar example's calculation day into the wide calendar example's requested day.
  Add the wide signed day to the wide calendar example's requested day.
  Answer the wide calendar example.

To calculate extended gate spacing for a wide signed day:
  \ A wide gap has no representable native signed-index field.
  \ Clear that field so an earlier native value is not mistaken for
  \ the current wide index by another caller.
  Put 0 into the gate inquiry's signed index.
  Put 0 into the gate inquiry's interval length.
  If the wide signed day's polarity is 0, exit.
  Prepare wide gate sauce counters given the wide signed day.
  Copy the wide calendar example into the sauce input.
  Make the complete sauce.
  Select the sealed gate interval.
